<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nanbu clan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Nanbu clan was a Japanese warrior family of northern Mutsu, descended from the Minamoto, which ruled from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morioka">Morioka</a> as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/daimyo">daimyo</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokugawa-shogunate">Tokugawa shogunate</a>. Confirmed in its lands by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toyotomi-hideyoshi">Toyotomi Hideyoshi</a> in 1590, it lost the Tsugaru region to its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsugaru-tamenobu">Ōura Tamenobu</a>, causing a lasting feud. After siding with the northern alliance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boshin-war">Boshin War</a> of 1868 its domain was reduced.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nanbu-clan.jpg" alt="Nanbu clan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mukai · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Japanese_Crest_Nanbu_Turu.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
